--TEST--
A class claiming `Parses` owes `format` beside `parse`, so a class that reads its text and cannot write it back is refused where it is declared — `rule:expressions/try-parse`, `rule:routing/link-target-and-params-are-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `format` writes the text that `parse` reads. This class has no `format`.
final class Slug implements Parses
{
    public tainted string $text = "";

    public function constructor(tainted string $text)
    {
        $this->text = $text;
    }

    public static function parse(tainted string $s): static
    {
        return new Slug($s);
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0449]: `Slug` does not declare `format`, which `Parses` requires
